[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 703,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 466,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 108307,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 542,
        "headingId": 466,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Sinonasal tract myxoma is a benign myofibroblastic proliferation within an extensively myxoid ground substance, arising in paranasal sinuses (not gnathic bone).</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-10T14:07:52"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 704,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 467,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 108308,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 542,
        "headingId": 467,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>8840/0 Sinonasal tract myxoma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-10T14:07:52"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 705,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 468,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 108309,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 542,
        "headingId": 468,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>2E90.6 &amp; XH6Q84 Benign neoplasm of nasopharynx &amp; Myxoma, NOS</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-10T14:07:52"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 706,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 469,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 108310,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 542,
        "headingId": 469,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Not recommended:</em> infantile odontogenic myxoma; peripheral odontogenic myxoma.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-10T14:07:52"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 707,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 470,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 108311,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 542,
        "headingId": 470,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-10T14:07:52"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 708,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 471,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 108312,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 542,
        "headingId": 471,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Sinonasal myxomas arise in the sinonasal region. They appear to arise in the soft tissue but may expand to involve adjacent bone.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-10T14:07:52"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 709,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 472,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 108313,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 542,
        "headingId": 472,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Sinonasal myxoma manifests as a slow-growing nasolabial swelling. Symptoms may be related to local tumour extension into the palate, orbit, and/or nasal cavity. Radiographically, sinonasal myxomas appear as well-defined, intraosseous, unilocular/multilocular radiolucencies. Tumours can be as large as 50&nbsp;mm {6302014; 21168253; 24429059; 15364495; 15701983; 27398121; 30484069}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-10T14:07:52"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 710,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 473,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 108314,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 542,
        "headingId": 473,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Sinonasal myxomas are rare, and they are reported almost exclusively in children aged &lt;&nbsp;3&nbsp;years (mean: 15&nbsp;months). There is a slight male predominance {8334970; 6302014; 21168253; 24429059; 15364495; 21624835; 15701983; 30484069}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-10T14:07:52"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 711,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 474,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 108315,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 542,
        "headingId": 474,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-10T14:07:52"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 712,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 475,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 108316,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 542,
        "headingId": 475,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The pathogenetic relationship between odontogenic myxoma and sinonasal myxoma is unclear {15364495; 21624835; 21168253; 30484069}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-10T14:07:52"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 719,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 482,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 108317,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 542,
        "headingId": 482,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Tumours have a grey-white, glistening surface and a gelatinous to firm consistency.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-10T14:07:52"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 713,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 476,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 108318,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 542,
        "headingId": 476,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Myxomas are similar no matter the site affected, showing a loose hypocellular proliferation of spindled, stellate, or round cells within a myxoid stroma containing arciform thin blood vessels and scattered fine collagen bands. Pleomorphism, mitotic figures, and tumour necrosis are absent {8334970; 6302014}. Odontogenic epithelium is absent {24429059; 30484069}. Immunohistochemistry is non-contributory, with variable SMA and nuclear &beta;-catenin positivity {30484069; 21624835}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-10T14:07:52"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 714,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 477,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 108319,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 542,
        "headingId": 477,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-10T14:07:52"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 715,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 478,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 108320,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 542,
        "headingId": 478,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-10T14:07:52"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 718,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 481,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 108321,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 542,
        "headingId": 481,
        "headingText": "<p><em>Essential:</em> a hypocellular proliferation of spindled/stellate cells forming a myxoid mass lesion of the sinonasal area not arising in gnathic bones.</p>\r\n<p><em>Desirable:</em> nuclear &beta;-catenin staining.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2023-05-04T17:51:26"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 716,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 479,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 108322,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 542,
        "headingId": 479,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-10T14:07:52"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 717,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 480,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 108323,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 542,
        "headingId": 480,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>These lesions are benign, but recurrence may be seen (in ~10% of cases) when incompletely removed {30484069; 21624835; 24429059; 6302014}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-10T14:07:52"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]